# =============================================================================
# RootLco — Root Link Company
# Example environment file. Copy to .env.local and fill in LOCAL values only.
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# NEVER commit .env, .env.local, or any file containing real values.
# NEVER put a production value in this file.
# Every value below is a placeholder or a well-known local default.
# =============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BROWSER-SAFE (NEXT_PUBLIC_*)
#
# Anything prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ is INLINED INTO THE BROWSER BUNDLE by Next.js
# and is therefore PUBLIC. Never give this prefix to a secret.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase API URL.
#   Host / browser  -> http://127.0.0.1:54321
#   From INSIDE the web container, 127.0.0.1 is the container itself, so the
#   compose file overrides this to http://host.docker.internal:54321.
#   See docs/phase-1/phase-1-1/docker-runbook.md ("Two hostnames, one Supabase").
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:54321

# Supabase anonymous key. Public BY DESIGN: it identifies the project, it does
# not authorise access. Its safety depends entirely on Row-Level Security.
#
#   RLS IS NOT YET IMPLEMENTED. No tenant-owned tables exist yet. RLS is a
#   mandatory Phase 1-2 gate (ADR-004). Do not treat this key as a control.
#
# Get the real local value with:  npm run supabase:status
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=paste-local-anon-key-from-supabase-status

# Which environment this build represents. One of: local | development | staging | production
# Only "local" is implemented. The others are Planned — not provisioned (ADR-012).
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_ENV=local

# Optional build identity, surfaced by /api/health. Injected by CI at image build.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_VERSION=0.1.0
# NEXT_PUBLIC_COMMIT_SHA=local

# Server log verbosity. One of: debug | info | warn | error.
# Read by src/server/observability/logger.ts. Unset or unrecognised falls back to
# the built-in default (quiet under test, info otherwise), so this is optional —
# but it is a real input to the running server and must be documented as one.
# LOG_LEVEL=info

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SERVER-ONLY — NEVER prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_
#
# These must never reach the browser. src/config/env.ts refuses to read them
# client-side, and src/lib/logging/logger.ts redacts them from logs.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Supabase service-role key. BYPASSES ROW-LEVEL SECURITY ENTIRELY.
#
#   Treat as a root credential. Never log it, never send it to the browser,
#   never commit it, never paste it into an issue.
#   Not required in Phase 1-1: no privileged server operation exists yet, and it
#   is deliberately not wired into src/lib/supabase/server.ts.
#
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Direct PostgreSQL connection. Local Supabase default shown; contains a password,
# so it is server-only. Not required by the app in Phase 1-1 (migrations use the CLI).
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:54322/postgres  # pragma: allowlist secret -- documented local Supabase CLI default, not a real credential

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ROTATION EXPECTATIONS
#
# - Local keys are generated by the Supabase CLI and are not secret across
#   developers; they are worthless outside your machine.
# - Any NON-LOCAL key must be rotated: on suspected exposure, immediately; when a
#   person with access leaves, immediately; otherwise on a schedule the owners set.
# - If a real secret is ever committed: ROTATE FIRST, then purge history. Do not
#   re-post the value anywhere — not in an issue, a PR, a log, or a report.
# - Reporting channel: see SECURITY.md.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
